![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

In `findObjectiveRef`, if the expected objective suffix is not found, the function silently falls back to the first objective in the array (`objectiveNodes[0]?.id`). This silent fallback can mask bugs or data extraction errors, leading to incorrect fixtures without triggering validation failures. It is safer to return `null` when the specific objective is not found so that the validation or test suite can explicitly catch the missing reference.

```suggestion
function findObjectiveRef(objectiveNodes, suffix) {
  const found = objectiveNodes.find((node) => node.id.endsWith(suffix))
  return found?.id ?? null
}
```
